---
import "../../styles/global.css";
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />

    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Microcosmos Atelier creates living aquatic ecosystems, thoughtfully designed around your space."
    />

    <title>Microcosmos Atelier — Living Aquatic Ecosystems</title>
  </head>

  <body>
    <!-- =====================================================
         HEADER
         ===================================================== -->

    <header class="site-header">
      <nav class="nav">
        <a href="/en/" class="logo">Microcosmos Atelier</a>

        <div class="navigation">
          <a href="/en/our-work">Our Work</a>
          <a href="/en/about">About</a>
          <a href="/en/contact">Contact</a>

          <div class="language-switcher">
            <a href="/">NL</a>
            <span>·</span>
            <a href="/en/" class="active">EN</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <main>
      <!-- =====================================================
           HERO
           ===================================================== -->

      <section class="hero">
        <img
          src="/images/hero/A002-3.jpeg"
          alt="A living aquatic ecosystem by Microcosmos Atelier"
          class="hero-image"
        />

        <div class="hero-overlay">
          <p class="eyebrow">Living aquatic ecosystems</p>

          <h1>
            A little piece<br />
            of nature, made yours.
          </h1>

          <p class="hero-text">
            I create living aquatic ecosystems designed around your space, your
            taste and the way you want to experience nature at home.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- =====================================================
           WHAT IS A MICROCOSMOS
           ===================================================== -->

      <section id="what-is-a-microcosmos" class="intro">
        <p class="eyebrow">What is a Microcosmos?</p>

        <h2>
          Not just an aquarium.<br />
          A little world of your own.
        </h2>

        <div class="intro-columns">
          <div>
            <p>
              A Microcosmos is a living ecosystem, thoughtfully designed and
              built to become part of your space.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <p>
              It brings together water, plants, wood, substrate, microorganisms,
              invertebrates and fish — not simply as decoration, but as parts of
              an interconnected system.
            </p>

            <p>
              You don't just look at it. You live alongside it. It grows,
              changes and evolves over time, becoming something that is uniquely
              yours.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- =====================================================
           THE IDEA
           ===================================================== -->

      <section class="section philosophy">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <p class="eyebrow">The idea</p>

          <h2>
            Creating something<br />
            that can find its own balance.
          </h2>
        </div>

        <div class="philosophy-content">
          <div class="philosophy-story">
            <p class="lead">
              Nature doesn't need to be perfected. It needs time, balance and
              the right conditions to unfold.
            </p>

            <p>That is the idea behind a Microcosmos.</p>

            <p>
              Rather than designing an aquarium as a finished composition, I
              create the conditions for a small living system to develop. Every
              part is connected through countless interactions that are often
              invisible, but constantly shaping the whole.
            </p>

            <p>
              The aim is not to control every detail. It is to find a natural
              balance between growth and restraint, abundance and scarcity,
              structure and change.
            </p>

            <p>And that takes patience.</p>

            <p>
              A newly built Microcosmos is only the beginning. Plants adapt,
              microorganisms establish themselves, animals explore their
              surroundings and relationships gradually emerge. What looks
              beautiful on day one can become something completely different —
              and often more beautiful — a year later.
            </p>

            <p>It is this process that makes each Microcosmos unique.</p>

            <p class="philosophy-highlight">
              Built with knowledge. Shaped by nature. Nurtured with patience and
              care.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="ecosystem-layers">
            <div>
              <span>01</span>
              <strong>Water</strong>
              <p>The medium connecting everything.</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <span>02</span>
              <strong>Plants</strong>
              <p>Growth, structure and transformation.</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <span>03</span>
              <strong>Substrate</strong>
              <p>A foundation for roots and microbial life.</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <span>04</span>
              <strong>Microorganisms</strong>
              <p>The invisible engine of the ecosystem.</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <span>05</span>
              <strong>Invertebrates</strong>
              <p>Grazers, recyclers and inhabitants.</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <span>06</span>
              <strong>Fish</strong>
              <p>Movement, behaviour and another layer of life.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- =====================================================
           INSPIRATION
           ===================================================== -->

      <section class="section inspiration">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <p class="eyebrow">Inspiration</p>

          <h2>
            Where would you<br />
            like to go?
          </h2>

          <p class="section-intro">
            A Microcosmos can take many forms. These images are visual
            interpretations created to explore different directions — they are
            inspiration, not photographs of existing projects.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="microcosmos-grid">
          <article class="microcosmos-card">
            <img
              src="/images/microcosmos/jungle-style.jpg"
              alt="Jungle-inspired Microcosmos"
            />

            <div class="card-content">
              <p class="eyebrow">Inspiration 01</p>

              <h3>Forest</h3>

              <p>
                Lush vegetation, layered greenery and the feeling of being
                immersed in a tropical forest.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article class="microcosmos-card">
            <img
              src="/images/microcosmos/amazon.jpg"
              alt="Amazon-inspired Microcosmos"
            />

            <div class="card-content">
              <p class="eyebrow">Inspiration 02</p>

              <h3>Littoral</h3>

              <p>
                The meeting of land and water — roots, vegetation, open water
                and natural transitions.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article class="microcosmos-card">
            <img
              src="/images/microcosmos/blackwater.jpg"
              alt="Blackwater-inspired Microcosmos"
            />

            <div class="card-content">
              <p class="eyebrow">Inspiration 03</p>

              <h3>Blackwater</h3>

              <p>
                Darker waters, natural tannins, wood and the quiet, mysterious
                atmosphere of tropical rivers.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article class="microcosmos-card">
            <img
              src="/images/microcosmos/custom.jpg"
              alt="Custom Microcosmos"
            />

            <div class="card-content">
              <p class="eyebrow">Inspiration 04</p>

              <h3>Your Own</h3>

              <p>
                Start with a place, a memory, an ecosystem — or simply a
                feeling.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- =====================================================
           HOW IT WORKS
           ===================================================== -->

      <section class="section process">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <p class="eyebrow">From idea to ecosystem</p>

          <h2>
            Designed around<br />
            your world.
          </h2>
        </div>

        <div class="process-list">
          <article>
            <span> 01 </span>

            <div>
              <h3>We start with your space</h3>

              <p>
                Where will it live? How much space is available? What is the
                light like? What do you want to feel when you look at it?
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article>
            <span> 02 </span>

            <div>
              <h3>We design the ecosystem</h3>

              <p>
                The layout, materials, plants and inhabitants are selected
                together, with both appearance and ecology in mind.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article>
            <span> 03 </span>

            <div>
              <h3>I build it</h3>

              <p>
                From substrate and structure to planting and introduction of
                life, everything is assembled as one coherent system.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article>
            <span> 04 </span>

            <div>
              <h3>Then it starts living</h3>

              <p>
                The ecosystem settles, grows and changes. Depending on the
                approach you choose, I can continue to follow and care for it
                with you.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- =====================================================
           HOW WE CAN WORK TOGETHER
           ===================================================== -->

      <section class="section formulas">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <p class="eyebrow">How we can work together</p>

          <h2>
            Choose how much<br />
            you want to be involved.
          </h2>

          <p class="section-intro">
            Every Microcosmos is different. Some people want the complete
            experience and then take it from there. Others want their ecosystem
            looked after over time.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="formula-list">
          <article>
            <span> 01 </span>

            <div>
              <h3>Design</h3>

              <p>
                We start with your space, your wishes and the kind of experience
                you want to create. Together we develop the concept, structure
                and character of your Microcosmos.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article>
            <span> 02 </span>

            <div>
              <h3>Curation</h3>

              <p>
                Plants, animals, materials and structure are carefully selected
                to create a coherent living system — one that is beautiful,
                functional and designed to develop over time.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article>
            <span> 03 </span>

            <div>
              <h3>Stewardship</h3>

              <p>
                Once established, your Microcosmos continues to grow and change.
                I can stay involved to help the ecosystem develop and keep it
                healthy over time.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article>
            <span> 04 </span>

            <div>
              <h3>Tailored</h3>

              <p>
                A completely bespoke approach for unusual spaces, ambitious
                installations or a very specific idea.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>
        </div>

        <a href="/en/contact" class="text-link"> Start a conversation → </a>
      </section>

      <!-- =====================================================
           OUR WORK
           ===================================================== -->

      <section class="section work-preview">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <p class="eyebrow">Our work</p>

          <h2>
            Real ecosystems.<br />
            Actually built.
          </h2>

          <p class="section-intro">
            A few examples of living systems I've designed and built over the
            years.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="work-grid">
          <img
            src="/images/our-work/A002-01.jpeg"
            alt="Fallen Forest Microcosmos"
          />

          <img
            src="/images/our-work/A003-01.jpeg"
            alt="Orinoco-inspired Littoral Zone Microcosmos"
          />

          <img
            src="/images/our-work/A004-01.jpeg"
            alt="Borneo Understory Microcosmos"
          />

          <img
            src="/images/our-work/A001-01.jpeg"
            alt="Shallow riverbed Microcosmos"
          />
        </div>

        <a href="/en/our-work" class="text-link"> Explore the projects → </a>
      </section>

      <!-- =====================================================
           ABOUT
           ===================================================== -->

      <section class="about">
        <div class="about-content">
          <p class="eyebrow">About</p>

          <h2>
            More than 35 years of exploring<br />
            underwater worlds.
          </h2>

          <p>
            What started as a childhood hobby slowly became a fascination with
            ecology — and with the incredible interactions between plants,
            animals, microorganisms, water and soil.
          </p>

          <p>
            Microcosmos Atelier grew from that fascination: a way of combining
            my interest in natural systems with my love for designing and
            building things.
          </p>

          <p class="about-highlight">
            Beautiful nature. Thoughtfully brought home.
          </p>

          <a href="/en/about"> More about me → </a>
        </div>

        <div class="about-image">
          <img src="/images/about/about.jpeg" alt="Kasper Masschaele" />
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- =====================================================
           FINAL CTA
           ===================================================== -->

      <section id="contact" class="cta">
        <p class="eyebrow">Your space. Your ecosystem.</p>

        <h2>Let's create something living.</h2>

        <p>
          You don't need to know exactly what you want. Bring me a space, an
          idea or simply a fascination with nature, and we'll start from there.
        </p>

        <a href="/en/contact" class="button dark-button">
          Start a conversation
        </a>
      </section>
    </main>

    <!-- =====================================================
         FOOTER
         ===================================================== -->

    <footer>
      <p>
        © {new Date().getFullYear()} Microcosmos Atelier
      </p>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
